# Valgrind suppressions for things inside Qt, so a run's output is about us.
#
# Only one entry so far, and it is worth being exact about why it is not ours:
# every frame is inside libQt6Core. QProcess starts a child through vforkfd,
# which reaps it with waitid() and a null infop -- legal, because it passes
# WNOWAIT and wants only the status, but Memcheck checks the pointer before it
# checks the flags and reports it against whichever test happened to spawn a
# process. It fires once per run regardless of what the test did afterwards.
#
# Anything else Memcheck reports is ours to look at.
{
   Qt QProcess: vforkfd reaps with a null waitid infop
   Memcheck:Param
   waitid(infop)
   fun:syscall
   fun:vforkfd
   ...
}
